    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9699-629X> ;
    skos:editorialNote "Electromagnetic Fields is \"fields representing the joint interplay of electric and magnetic forces\", which is what this concept models as a medium."@en .

sstim-ex:mediumElectromagneticField skos:closeMatch wd:Q177625 .

[] a owl:Axiom ;
    owl:annotatedSource sstim-ex:mediumElectromagneticField ;
    owl:annotatedProperty skos:closeMatch ;
    owl:annotatedTarget wd:Q177625 ;
    dct:source <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q177625> ;
    dct:date "2026-09-06"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9699-629X> ;
    skos:editorialNote "The physical field produced by charged objects, which this concept treats as an exposure medium."@en .

sstim-ex:mediumElectromagneticRadiation skos:closeMatch mesh:D060733 .

[] a owl:Axiom ;
    owl:annotatedSource sstim-ex:mediumElectromagneticRadiation ;
    owl:annotatedProperty skos:closeMatch ;
    owl:annotatedTarget mesh:D060733 ;
    dct:source <http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D060733> ;
    dct:date "2026-09-06"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9699-629X> ;
    skos:editorialNote "Described there as waves of oscillating electric and magnetic fields moving outward from the source, which is this concept's referent."@en .

sstim-ex:mediumAppliedMagneticField skos:closeMatch mesh:D060526 .

[] a owl:Axiom ;
    owl:annotatedSource sstim-ex:mediumAppliedMagneticField ;
    owl:annotatedProperty skos:closeMatch ;
    owl:annotatedTarget mesh:D060526 ;
    dct:source <http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D060526> ;
    dct:date "2026-09-06"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9699-629X> ;
    skos:editorialNote "Magnetic Fields is \"areas of attractive or repulsive force surrounding magnets\". This concept additionally requires that the field be applied by a coil or magnet as the delivered medium."@en .

sstim-ex:mediumAppliedMagneticField skos:closeMatch wd:Q11408 .

[] a owl:Axiom ;
    owl:annotatedSource sstim-ex:mediumAppliedMagneticField ;
    owl:annotatedProperty skos:closeMatch ;
    owl:annotatedTarget wd:Q11408 ;
    dct:source <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q11408> ;
    dct:date "2026-09-06"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9699-629X> ;
    skos:editorialNote "The physics concept, without the applied-as-medium requirement."@en .

sstim-ex:mediumAppliedElectricCurrent skos:broadMatch mesh:D004560 .

[] a owl:Axiom ;
    owl:annotatedSource sstim-ex:mediumAppliedElectricCurrent ;
    owl:annotatedProperty skos:broadMatch ;
    owl:annotatedTarget mesh:D004560 ;
    dct:source <http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D004560> ;
    dct:date "2026-09-06"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9699-629X> ;
    skos:editorialNote "MeSH Electricity spans \"the physical effects involving the presence of electric charges at rest and in motion\", so it includes electrostatics that this concept, which requires current through electrodes in contact with tissue, excludes."@en .

sstim-ex:mediumAppliedElectricCurrent skos:closeMatch wd:Q11651 .

[] a owl:Axiom ;
    owl:annotatedSource sstim-ex:mediumAppliedElectricCurrent ;
    owl:annotatedProperty skos:closeMatch ;
    owl:annotatedTarget wd:Q11651 ;
    dct:source <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q11651> ;
    dct:date "2026-09-06"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9699-629X> ;
    skos:editorialNote "Electric current specifically, which is what this concept delivers, minus the through-electrodes requirement."@en .

sstim-ex:mediumAirflow skos:closeMatch mesh:D000392 .

[] a owl:Axiom ;
    owl:annotatedSource sstim-ex:mediumAirflow ;
    owl:annotatedProperty skos:closeMatch ;
    owl:annotatedTarget mesh:D000392 ;
    dct:source <http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D000392> ;
    dct:date "2026-09-06"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9699-629X> ;
    skos:editorialNote "Air Movements is \"the motion of air currents\". This concept adds the purpose, a tactile, thermal or proximity cue, which is an intension difference and not an extension one. Deliberately not the exact-label Wikidata item wd:Q4698686, which is airflow as a measurement rather than moving air."@en .

sstim-ex:mediumOlfactoryChemicalExposure skos:relatedMatch mesh:D009812 .

[] a owl:Axiom ;
    owl:annotatedSource sstim-ex:mediumOlfactoryChemicalExposure ;
    owl:annotatedProperty skos:relatedMatch ;
    owl:annotatedTarget mesh:D009812 ;
    dct:source <http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D009812> ;
    dct:date "2026-09-06"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9699-629X> ;
    skos:editorialNote "Odorants names the volatile substances; this concept names an exposure. Different kinds of thing, the same distinction that keeps the multisensory-integration and synaptic-transmission mappings at related."@en .

sstim-ex:mediumPharmacologicalAgent skos:closeMatch mesh:D004364 .

[] a owl:Axiom ;
    owl:annotatedSource sstim-ex:mediumPharmacologicalAgent ;
    owl:annotatedProperty skos:closeMatch ;
    owl:annotatedTarget mesh:D004364 ;
    dct:source <http://id.nlm.nih.gov/mesh/D004364> ;
    dct:date "2026-09-06"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9699-629X> ;
    skos:editorialNote "Pharmaceutical Preparations requires a finished dosage form, which this concept does not, while both name the substance delivered as the controlled input."@en .

sstim-ex:mediumThermalEnergy skos:closeMatch wd:Q209233 .

[] a owl:Axiom ;
    owl:annotatedSource sstim-ex:mediumThermalEnergy ;
    owl:annotatedProperty skos:closeMatch ;
    owl:annotatedTarget wd:Q209233 ;
    dct:source <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q209233> ;
    dct:date "2026-09-06"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9699-629X> ;
    skos:editorialNote "Thermal energy as internal energy due to temperature, which is what this concept applies as a stimulus. MeSH splits the same ground across Hot Temperature and Cold Temperature, neither of which alone corresponds, so no MeSH row is asserted."@en .


###########################################################################
# Signal shapes, audio noise colours and study designs — tranche 3
# (2026-09-07)
#
# Wikidata carries this tranche alone, and the reason is worth stating because
# it is not shyness about MeSH. MeSH's study-design descriptors are publication
# types: D016449 describes an article reporting a randomised trial, not the
# design of the study it reports. This vocabulary classifies the design of a
# source study inside an evidence assessment, so the Wikidata method items are
# the right subject and the MeSH ones are a neighbouring one.
#
# Two rows exist to avoid a better-matching label. shapeNoise maps to the
# signal-processing sense and not to wd:Q179448, noise as unwanted sound;
# shapeEnvelope maps to the waveform envelope and not to wd:Q170124, the
# stationery item that a label search returns first.
#
# The four principal noise colours map to items Wikidata itself groups under
# colors of noise, so the family is coherent on both sides. Blue and violet are
# thin items with no description, and carry the same reservation already
# recorded for monaural beats.
#
# Not mapped: shapeSampled, designMixedDesigns, designUnknownDesign and
# designPreclinicalExperiment. The first three are bookkeeping values with no
# external counterpart, and the fourth's nearest item, wd:Q7239206, is
# preclinical development as a drug-development stage rather than an
# experimental design.
###########################################################################

sstim-v:shapeSine skos:closeMatch wd:Q207527 .

[] a owl:Axiom ;
    owl:annotatedSource sstim-v:shapeSine ;
    owl:annotatedProperty skos:closeMatch ;
    owl:annotatedTarget wd:Q207527 ;
    dct:source <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q207527> ;
    dct:date "2026-09-07"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9699-629X> ;
    skos:editorialNote "The item is the sinusoid itself, a mathematical curve; this concept is the controlled value naming that shape as a signal's form. Under ADR 0021 a controlled value is an information category rather than the entity it classifies, so closeMatch is the strongest defensible relation here, as it was for the neural systems."@en .

sstim-v:shapeSquare skos:closeMatch wd:Q1136640 .

[] a owl:Axiom ;
    owl:annotatedSource sstim-v:shapeSquare ;
    owl:annotatedProperty skos:closeMatch ;
    owl:annotatedTarget wd:Q1136640 ;
    dct:source <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q1136640> ;
    dct:date "2026-09-07"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9699-629X> ;
    skos:editorialNote "The waveform alternating between two levels. Same category-versus-entity reasoning as the sine row; the item carries no duty-cycle boundary, which this concept's definition does."@en .

sstim-v:shapeTriangle skos:closeMatch wd:Q1257456 .

[] a owl:Axiom ;
    owl:annotatedSource sstim-v:shapeTriangle ;
    owl:annotatedProperty skos:closeMatch ;
    owl:annotatedTarget wd:Q1257456 ;
    dct:source <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q1257456> ;
    dct:date "2026-09-07"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9699-629X> ;
    skos:editorialNote "The waveform rising and falling linearly. Same reasoning as the sine and square rows."@en .

sstim-v:shapeSawtooth skos:closeMatch wd:Q1742397 .

[] a owl:Axiom ;
    owl:annotatedSource sstim-v:shapeSawtooth ;
    owl:annotatedProperty skos:closeMatch ;
    owl:annotatedTarget wd:Q1742397 ;
    dct:source <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q1742397> ;
    dct:date "2026-09-07"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9699-629X> ;
    skos:editorialNote "The waveform rising linearly and resetting sharply. Same reasoning; the item does not distinguish the mirrored ramp, which this concept admits."@en .

sstim-v:shapeNoise skos:closeMatch wd:Q17104942 .

[] a owl:Axiom ;
    owl:annotatedSource sstim-v:shapeNoise ;
    owl:annotatedProperty skos:closeMatch ;
    owl:annotatedTarget wd:Q17104942 ;
    dct:source <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q17104942> ;
    dct:date "2026-09-07"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9699-629X> ;
    skos:editorialNote "Deliberately the signal-processing sense, \"unwanted modifications to a signal\", and not wd:Q179448, which is noise as unwanted sound. This concept is a stochastic signal occupying a frequency extent, so the acoustic sense would be the wrong subject even though its label matches better."@en .

sstim-v:shapeEnvelope skos:closeMatch wd:Q5380913 .

[] a owl:Axiom ;
    owl:annotatedSource sstim-v:shapeEnvelope ;
    owl:annotatedProperty skos:closeMatch ;
    owl:annotatedTarget wd:Q5380913 ;
    dct:source <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q5380913> ;
    dct:date "2026-09-07"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9699-629X> ;
    skos:editorialNote "The item is the function describing the extremes of an oscillating signal, which is what this concept names as a non-repeating contour over time. Deliberately not wd:Q170124, the stationery item, which the label search returned first."@en .

sstim-ex:audioNoiseWhite skos:closeMatch wd:Q381287 .

[] a owl:Axiom ;
    owl:annotatedSource sstim-ex:audioNoiseWhite ;
    owl:annotatedProperty skos:closeMatch ;
    owl:annotatedTarget wd:Q381287 ;
    dct:source <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q381287> ;
    dct:date "2026-09-07"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9699-629X> ;
    skos:editorialNote "Equal intensity at different frequencies, which is this concept's flat spectrum. One of four rows whose targets Wikidata itself groups under colors of noise (P31 Q4854529), so the family is coherent on both sides."@en .

sstim-ex:audioNoisePink skos:closeMatch wd:Q974572 .

[] a owl:Axiom ;
    owl:annotatedSource sstim-ex:audioNoisePink ;
    owl:annotatedProperty skos:closeMatch ;
    owl:annotatedTarget wd:Q974572 ;
    dct:source <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q974572> ;
    dct:date "2026-09-07"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9699-629X> ;
    skos:editorialNote "Amplitude inversely proportional to frequency, which is this concept's equal power per octave."@en .

sstim-ex:audioNoiseBrownRed skos:closeMatch wd:Q1437483 .

[] a owl:Axiom ;
    owl:annotatedSource sstim-ex:audioNoiseBrownRed ;
    owl:annotatedProperty skos:closeMatch ;
    owl:annotatedTarget wd:Q1437483 ;
    dct:source <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q1437483> ;
    dct:date "2026-09-07"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9699-629X> ;
    skos:editorialNote "Brownian noise, the signal noise produced by Brownian motion, which is the roughly 6 dB per octave fall this concept names. The label differs from ours, brown and red being the same colour convention."@en .

sstim-ex:audioNoiseGrey skos:closeMatch wd:Q2380254 .

[] a owl:Axiom ;
    owl:annotatedSource sstim-ex:audioNoiseGrey ;
    owl:annotatedProperty skos:closeMatch ;
    owl:annotatedTarget wd:Q2380254 ;
    dct:source <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q2380254> ;
    dct:date "2026-09-07"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9699-629X> ;
    skos:editorialNote "Noise following a psychoacoustic equal-loudness contour, which is this concept's definition almost word for word."@en .

sstim-ex:audioNoiseBlue skos:closeMatch wd:Q12345729 .

[] a owl:Axiom ;
    owl:annotatedSource sstim-ex:audioNoiseBlue ;
    owl:annotatedProperty skos:closeMatch ;
    owl:annotatedTarget wd:Q12345729 ;
    dct:source <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q12345729> ;
    dct:date "2026-09-07"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9699-629X> ;
    skos:editorialNote "A thin item: it names the colour and carries neither description nor type, so closeMatch is the strongest defensible assertion, as it is for monaural beats."@en .

sstim-ex:audioNoiseVioletPurple skos:closeMatch wd:Q31073746 .

[] a owl:Axiom ;
    owl:annotatedSource sstim-ex:audioNoiseVioletPurple ;
    owl:annotatedProperty skos:closeMatch ;
    owl:annotatedTarget wd:Q31073746 ;
    dct:source <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q31073746> ;
    dct:date "2026-09-07"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9699-629X> ;
    skos:editorialNote "Typed as noise on Wikidata but carrying no description, so the same reservation as the blue row applies."@en .

sstim-ex:audioNoiseBlackSilence skos:closeMatch wd:Q502261 .

[] a owl:Axiom ;
    owl:annotatedSource sstim-ex:audioNoiseBlackSilence ;
    owl:annotatedProperty skos:closeMatch ;
    owl:annotatedTarget wd:Q502261 ;
    dct:source <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q502261> ;
    dct:date "2026-09-07"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9699-629X> ;
    skos:editorialNote "Silence as the lack of audible sound. This concept additionally covers muting and the deliberate absence of an intended stimulus, which is a stimulation-context extension rather than a different subject."@en .

sstim-v:designRandomizedControlledTrial skos:closeMatch wd:Q1436668 .

[] a owl:Axiom ;
    owl:annotatedSource sstim-v:designRandomizedControlledTrial ;
    owl:annotatedProperty skos:closeMatch ;
    owl:annotatedTarget wd:Q1436668 ;
    dct:source <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q1436668> ;
    dct:date "2026-09-07"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9699-629X> ;
    skos:editorialNote "The item is the experimental method, which is what this concept classifies. Deliberately not MeSH D016449, which is a publication type describing an article rather than the design of the study it reports; the same reason no MeSH row appears on any concept in this scheme."@en .

sstim-v:designObservational skos:closeMatch wd:Q818574 .

[] a owl:Axiom ;
    owl:annotatedSource sstim-v:designObservational ;
    owl:annotatedProperty skos:closeMatch ;
    owl:annotatedTarget wd:Q818574 ;
    dct:source <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q818574> ;
    dct:date "2026-09-07"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9699-629X> ;
    skos:editorialNote "A study drawing inferences without experimenter-controlled allocation, which is this concept's definition."@en .

sstim-v:designControlledTrial skos:broadMatch wd:Q70447452 .

[] a owl:Axiom ;
    owl:annotatedSource sstim-v:designControlledTrial ;
    owl:annotatedProperty skos:broadMatch ;
    owl:annotatedTarget wd:Q70447452 ;
    dct:source <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q70447452> ;
    dct:date "2026-09-07"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9699-629X> ;
    skos:editorialNote "The item is a controlled clinical trial with at least one control group and does not exclude randomised allocation, while this concept is explicitly the non-randomised case. The item is therefore broader, and asserting closeMatch would erase the distinction the scheme exists to draw."@en .

sstim-v:designCaseReport skos:closeMatch wd:Q2782326 .

[] a owl:Axiom ;
    owl:annotatedSource sstim-v:designCaseReport ;
    owl:annotatedProperty skos:closeMatch ;
    owl:annotatedTarget wd:Q2782326 ;
    dct:source <http://www.wikidata.org/entity/Q2782326> ;
    dct:date "2026-09-07"^^xsd:date ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9699-629X> ;
    skos:editorialNote "The item describes itself as a publication type, while this concept is a study design in an evidence assessment. The extension is nearly the same, since a case report is reported as one, so close rather than exact, with the framing difference recorded rather than smoothed."@en .

